      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This behavior is likely due to finding the knife \"smoked\" by over-steelying with a dull tip, which causes the grain to tear unpredictably rather than the tool taking a clean cut. Correction involves beginning your final chisel sharpening with a 15° wedge angle instead of a standard bevel, then swapping to a 20° bevel once the knife becomes smoke-free. Finally, verify your pin's mouth angle against the template's corresponding angle to ensure the knife sits correctly against the wood before making contact.",
